{"id": "EUVD-2026-96697", "enisaUuid": "aab4e459-692a-3e84-9320-5942aaf386d7", "description": "ConvertX through 0.19.0 contains an arbitrary file read vulnerability that allows authenticated users to read server files because src/converters/pandoc.ts invokes Pandoc without the --sandbox flag. Attackers can upload a reStructuredText document with an include directive naming an absolute path, convert it, and download output containing the referenced file's contents.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T01:35:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:53:07", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/C4illin/ConvertX/issues/668", "https://github.com/C4illin/ConvertX", "https://github.com/C4illin/ConvertX/blob/710bc7c71712af04198a39f003e3ea1aa5168a31/src/converters/pandoc.ts#L123-L152", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/convertx-through-0.19.0-arbitrary-file-read-via-pandoc-converter"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r4xg-82px-pwx6", "CVE-2026-108694"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e8c9367d-02b8-3cee-a42c-bf81ceb1ddf8", "product": {"name": "ConvertX", "vendor": {"name": "C4illin"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.19.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e6a9d5d6-c54d-39af-89bd-b786bcd03f8e", "vendor": {"name": "C4illin"}}], "isExploited": false}